     "type": "SECTION_HEADING",
     "group": "MAIN",
     "text": "1 Introduction",
     "in_flow": 1,
     "in_side": null,
     "ok": true
    },
    {
     "type": "BODY",
     "group": "MAIN",
     "text": "Reports of the presence of expansive soils and the associated consequences",
     "in_flow": 1,
     "in_side": null,
     "ok": true
    },
    {
     "type": "BODY",
     "group": "MAIN",
     "text": "The soil-water retention curve (SWRC) is known to be dependent on sample density",
     "in_flow": 1,
     "in_side": null,
     "ok": true
    },
    {
     "type": "SECTION_HEADING",
     "group": "MAIN",
     "text": "2 Unsaturated expansive clays",
     "in_flow": 1,
     "in_side": null,
     "ok": true
    },
    {
     "type": "BODY",
     "group": "MAIN",
     "text": "Expansive clays exhibit large volume changes with changes in water content",
     "in_flow": 1,
     "in_side": null,
     "ok": true
    },
    {
     "type": "BODY",
     "group": "MAIN",
     "text": "partially saturated soils to predict heaving of swelling clays",
     "in_flow": 1,
     "in_side": null,
     "ok": true
    },
    {
     "type": "BODY",
     "group": "MAIN",
     "text": "The selected site near Vredefort, South Africa is underlain",
     "in_flow": 1,
     "in_side": null,
     "ok": true
    },
    {
     "type": "CAPTION",
     "group": "MAIN",
     "text": "Fig. 2. Simplified borehole log of selected site.",
     "in_flow": 1,
     "in_side": null,
     "ok": true
    },
    {
     "type": "CAPTION",
     "group": "MAIN",
     "text": "Table 1. Properties of the expansive clay sampled at 3.0 m.",
     "in_flow": 1,
     "in_side": null,
     "ok": true
    },
    {
     "type": "SECTION_HEADING",
     "group": "MAIN",
     "text": "5 Results and discussion",
     "in_flow": 1,
     "in_side": null,
     "ok": true
    },
    {
     "type": "SECTION_HEADING",
     "group": "MAIN",
     "text": "6 Conclusions",
     "in_flow": 1,
     "in_side": null,
     "ok": true
    },
    {
     "type": "BODY",
     "group": "MAIN",
     "text": "Gravimetric water content soil-water retention curves in this study were found to be nearly independent",
